Even older than Java, Python has achieved a lot of popularity in
recent years. It is an easy-to-learn general purpose programming language,
with strong capabilities, including in state-of-the-art topics such as machine learning and
artificial intelligence. In this article we want to present scenarios where 
\LaTeX\ and Python can work jointly. We will show 
examples where \LaTeX\ documents are automatically generated by 
Python or receive content from Python scripts.
